     "<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Dear all,</p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">We are pleased to announce the 5th edition of the Physalia online course: <strong>R/Bioconductor for Mass Spectrometry and Proteomics</strong></p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Dates: 17–19 November</p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Course website: <a href=\"https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/course58/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" title=\"This external link will open in a new window\" style=\"color:rgb(0,102,204);outline:none\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/course58/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793230308332000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2l5uzq6pv0JYPeg7zyl6rG\">https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/course58/</a></p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">This three-day workshop, run in partnership with Bioconductor Training, will introduce participants to the analysis of mass spectrometry-based proteomics data in R/Bioconductor. Through a combination of lectures and hands-on tutorials, participants will learn how to:</p><ul style=\"font-family:georgia;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><li><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-size:10pt;word-wrap:break-word\">Manipulate and visualise raw MS data</p></li><li><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-size:10pt;word-wrap:break-word\">Work with identification and quantitation data</p></li><li><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-size:10pt;word-wrap:break-word\">Apply statistical methods to identify differentially expressed proteins</p></li></ul><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">The course is designed for proteomics practitioners and data analysts familiar with R, looking to gain practical skills in MS data analysis using Bioconductor tools.</p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">For the full list of our courses and workshops, please visit: <a href=\"https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/course58/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" title=\"This external link will open in a new window\" style=\"color:rgb(0,102,204);outline:none;font-size:13.333333015441895px\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/course58/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793230308332000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2l5uzq6pv0JYPeg7zyl6rG\">https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/</a></p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Best regards,</p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Carlo</p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;trebuchet ms&quot;;font-size:10pt\">--------------------<br><br>Carlo Pecoraro, Ph.D<br><br><br>Physalia-courses DIRECTOR<br><br><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">in...@physalia-courses.org</a><br><br>mobile: <a href=\"tel:+49%20176%2045230846\" value=\"+4917645230846\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+49 17645230846</a><br><br><a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/physaliacourses.bsky.social\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" title=\"This external link will open in a new window\" style=\"color:rgb(0,102,204);outline:none\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://bsky.app/profile/physaliacourses.bsky.social&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793230308332000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3duZmI18gBgRs9T8Vib92P\">Bluesky</a> <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/physalia-courses-a64418127/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" title=\"This external link will open in a new window\" style=\"color:rgb(0,102,204);outline:none\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.linkedin.com/in/physalia-courses-a64418127/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793230308332000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0FRldxYJr148yIEmkM0mL3\">Linkedin</a></p>"
